The gate's trees, scripts and outputs are read-forbidden (`.tools/b748*`, `wt-b748-*`); you rebuild from its STATUS lines 122-132 (the method and the groups) and from the shape descriptions above. Method (copy the gate's, it is the right one): original bytes' sha256 checked before (`PurchaseValidation.cs` prefix `666064b9`, RELAYED); every anchor asserted EXACTLY once (line context printed); the edit written and read back; the Api test project built Release at **0 warnings** (a warning is BROKEN: use a discard read, e.g. `_ = x;`, to keep an unused counter quiet); the filter `FullyQualifiedName~QuoteApiTests.WalkCap` run (DevStub; the validation does not depend on the provider; your NEW rows' Entra copies are run in the baseline and in the final CI line); the original bytes written back and the sha256 proved equal; `git status --porcelain` of `wt-b754-mut` 0 lines after each job. About 20 s per variant. The groups (a)-(k) of the gate (line 124): (a) each of the five counters and the supplies budget initialised from the fleet text walk (`Math.Min(MaxWalkEntriesListed, <fleet sites with a control character>)`) and from the repeated-number walk (`<fleet numbers used more than once>`); (b) pairs of the five sharing one counter, each of the five on the section id's counter, the supplies budget on each of the six BOM counters; (c) the line-number entry advancing another counter (g03) and a counter skipping lines numbered below 1 (g04); (d) `<=` and `< 19` on all six guards, the constant 21 and 19; (e) `Listed`: no `Math.Min`, `- listed + 1`, `- listed - 1`, `RemoveRange` start and count off by one both ways, `listed += errors.Count - before`, `listed++` per line seen, a pair counted once, the section-id shape on each pair field, a local copy instead of the ref; (f) names-exactly-one on its own counter, outside the guard, order swapped; (g) per-line-seen counters; (h) the cap removed from each field, guard-only removal on the pair fields; (i) the supplies walk: budget per list, per call site, per click rate, `<=`, `< 19`, `- 1`, the count error counted, the required entry counted, the loop bound dropped, the increment dropped; (k) seeded one-character edits (seed of your choice, recorded; a BROKEN or anchor-refused draw is redrawn and said). **Add your own** (a) the supplies budget wired on ONE call site only to a BOM counter (the click-rate site; the usage site), (b) the required entry suppressed once the budget is spent (`if (nullsListed < MaxWalkEntriesListed)` around its `errors.Add`), (c) the two-fleet-walk seeds with a count smaller than 20 (so a row built on a full walk cannot hide a half-seeded one). **Not in scope:** group (j) (quantity `<= 0`, `< 1`, `>=`; line number `<= 1`, `< 0`) belongs to B748-5 / Note N6: run the group if you like, say what it reads, build nothing for `j-qty-ge`.
